  "description": "<p>Currently, the value of DSLocation for managed datastreams is assumed to follow a particular scheme in serializers and deserializers, and elsewhere.  These assumptions should be removed, and DSLocation should be simply passed on as an opaque value wherever possible.   For example, several deserializers generate DSLocation values for managed datastreams as \"PID + DSID + DSVersionID\" (an assumption) rather than re-using the serialized value (treating it as opaque). </p>",
